From 8f23f4e26a5a80e68ca3b4ac72ca9948b0bfe022 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Corin McHargue <corin.mchargue@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 2 Nov 2026 16:32:44 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(worktree): allow an external provider command to manage
 worktrees

Add [worktree] provider_command and TUIOS_WORKTREES_PROVIDER_COMMAND.
When set (or when HERDR_WORKTREES_PROVIDER_COMMAND is in the environment),
tuios delegates worktree creation, listing, and removal to the external
provider through the JSON contract (detect, resolve, create, list,
remove).

Repositories not claimed by the provider fall back to native git
worktrees and [worktree] path.

Provider calls are bounded and checked:
- detect answers are cached per repository for five minutes
- resolve pre-checks taken folders and picks free fan branch names
- create and remove run one at a time
- create must return an absolute path to a git checkout
- query calls time out after 30s, create/remove after 20m, and a timeout
  ends the provider's process group
- list falls back to git worktree list when the provider fails
- config validation warns when the command is not executable
